[3b] Regression diagnostics (linearity, homoscedasticity, normality)...
  --- Regression diagnostics (autosomal training genes, Human cardiac fibroblast (ribonn)) ---
  Normality of TE (actual, log2 scale, n=9,599): skew = 0.283, excess kurtosis = 0.568, D'Agostino K^2 p = 5.3e-45, Jarque-Bera p = 1.55e-56
  Normality of residuals: skew = 0.114, excess kurtosis = 0.739, D'Agostino K^2 p = 1.92e-31, Jarque-Bera p = 1.16e-52
  Homoscedasticity (Breusch-Pagan): LM stat = 180.473, p = 9.55e-14
  Linearity (Ramsey RESET, power=3 on fitted values): F = 38.924, p = 1.46e-17
  (in each test, p < 0.05 => reject the null of normality / homoscedasticity / linearity)
